.SH NAME
ktm-config \- Environment variables and a .env file into a struct: @env, @required, defaults.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.EX
import config;
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Environment variables and a .env file into a struct: @env, @required, defaults.
.SH CONSTANTS
.SS ERR_CONFIG
.EX
0x6B746D23
.EE
.PP
What fromEnv and loadDotenv throw: the message names every variable that is missing or wrong
.SH FUNCTIONS
.SS snakeUpper
.EX
String snakeUpper(u8[] name);
.EE
.PP
databaseUrl -> DATABASE_URL, httpURL -> HTTP_URL, URLPath -> URL_PATH
.SS fromEnv
.EX
void fromEnv(reflect.Value v, u8[] prefix = "");
.EE
.PP
Fills the struct v (reflect.of(settings)) from the environment: each field whose variable is set; the others keep what they hold (a default). Throws ERR_CONFIG naming every variable that is missing (@required), can't be read or breaks a rule of validate's, after setting the rest. u8[] fields are views of the environment's values, String fields copies (config.free frees them).
.SS free
.EX
void free(reflect.Value v);
.EE
.PP
Frees the String fields of the struct v (nested ones too)
.SS loadDotenv
.EX
i64 loadDotenv(u8[] path = ".env", bool override = false);
.EE
.PP
Sets the variables in the .env file at path: \fBKEY=value\fR lines, \fBexport KEY=value\fR, # comments, "double quotes" (with \en, \et, \e", \e\e and ${OTHER} expanded) and 'single quotes' (as written); an unquoted value ends at \fB #\fR\&. A variable that is already set keeps its value unless override. Answers how many it set, -1 when there is no such file; a line it can't read throws ERR_CONFIG with its number.
